WEBVTT

00:00:00.450 --> 00:00:05.664
Log in. Download. Copy. Paste. Send.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:09.697
Every week, the same clicks.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:14.264
Teach it once. From tomorrow, it's AI's job.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.117
Just tell Kitewell what you do, in plain words.

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:25.381
It lays out every step, for you to check.

00:00:29.100 --> 00:00:34.190
Then it does the clicking — on websites, desktop apps, and email.

00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.002
Even the old app nothing else can talk to.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:40.350
It stops for your OK where it matters.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.345
And it keeps a record of every step.

00:00:45.550 --> 00:00:46.900
Got a list in Excel?

00:00:46.950 --> 00:00:50.871
It runs for every row, and writes each result back beside it.

00:00:50.950 --> 00:00:54.330
It learns the clicks once, then repeats them every weekday —

00:00:54.430 --> 00:00:56.910
and relearns them if a page changes.

00:00:57.860 --> 00:01:00.810
Prefer code? It's plain YAML underneath.

00:01:00.860 --> 00:01:05.920
Run scripts, containers, and coding agents like Claude Code and Codex.

00:01:05.970 --> 00:01:09.026
Or build it all from your own agent, over MCP.

00:01:09.260 --> 00:01:10.967
It all runs on your own computer.

00:01:12.100 --> 00:01:14.810
What you teach becomes the whole team's knowledge.

00:01:15.230 --> 00:01:17.455
The more you use it, the less you explain.

00:01:18.260 --> 00:01:20.180
Your passwords stay on your machine.

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:21.722
Kitewell.

00:01:22.410 --> 00:01:23.690
It flies on its own.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:24.956
You hold the string.
